  "readOnlyHint": true,
  "title": "Resolve a ticker to its token page"
 },
 "description": "Resolve a ticker to its token page\n\nThe token page's own lookup (it backs `{symbol}.crown.info` and `chaindaddy.io/{symbol}`): the one registration that page shows for a ticker, with its profile metadata, market data, DEX pair and on-chain trust row (LP lock or burn, authorities). `chain` (a chain key such as `base`, a chain name, or a CAIP-2 id) and `idx` narrow it.\n\nWhen nothing is registered it may still return an unregistered token for the ticker (`crown.status: unclaimed`). A 200 with no `crown` object at all means there is no token page for the ticker. `canonicalPath` is the URL path (`/{chain}`) the page lives at. `totalCrowns` / `chainCrowns` count the ticker's registrations overall and on the chain.\n\nCached up to 30 minutes; `cached: true` marks a cached answer. Needs an API key unless called from the Chain Daddy website.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "chain": {
    "description": "Chain key (`base`), chain name, or CAIP-2 id (`eip155:8453`).",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "idx": {
    "description": "1-based position among the ticker's registrations (within `chain` when given), to pick one peer.",
    "minimum": 1,
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "symbol": {
    "description": "Token ticker, case-insensitive (e.g. `PEPE`).",
    "examples": [
     "PEPE"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "symbol"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "resolve_token_page",
